Expose the peer-to-peer connection classes on the lib default export

Why: a node serving peers has to attach each inbound WebSocket and each
message posted over HTTP to the switch with the switch's own connection
classes, checked by the switch's own peer parser, and has to accept the
WebSocket with the same "ws" server, and the same frame bound, that the
switch's dialer uses, so none of them may be ported.
Upstream status: the package exports only the switch (lib.P2P). Module 7074
(p2p) is already imported by the lib default export (module 8568), and its
default import is the module itself, since the module is an ES module, so its
P2PWebSocket, P2PHttpConnection, P2PPeerFromJSO and
P2P_WEBSOCKET_MAX_PAYLOAD_BYTES are reached through that import. The bundled
"ws" 8.21.3, module 7699, is imported and its WebSocketServer exposed. All
are typed in client/index.d.ts as lib/p2p.d.ts declares them, and the server
as lib/p2p.d.ts types the socket, through "ws". P2PHttpConnection is exposed
as HTTPConnection, since the code that reads it capitalizes initialisms.
Removal condition: upstream exports these names, then delete this patch and
import them from the public entry points.

Applies with "patch -p1" from the package root, after 0001 and 0002.

